<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Salian Franks</h1><p class="st-meta">358 CE – 481 CE (approx.) · capital Tournai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Frankish group settled in Toxandria by Rome in 358, whose kings at Tournai founded the Merovingian dynasty.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Salians were one of the Frankish peoples living near the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. In 358 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-emperor">Caesar Julian</a> forced the submission of those who had settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toxandria">Toxandria</a>, in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campine">Kempen</a>, and let them remain as allies of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>. Over the next century they moved south-west towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their kings served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> as federate commanders. Around the 440s King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodio">Chlodio</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-cambrai">Cambrai</a> and the land up to the Somme. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salic-law">Lex Salica</a>, written down under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a>, preserves their customary law, including the rule later used to bar women from the French throne.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childeric-i">Childeric I</a>, traditionally the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merovech">Merovech</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tournai">Tournai</a> and fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>; his rich tomb, found in 1653, held a signet ring and gold bees. On his death in 481 his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> began the conquests that created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 358 CE – 481 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:66.83%;width:2.45%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>358 CE – 481 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tournai</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Chlodio, Childeric I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Germanic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Frankish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Tournai</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=420&amp;focus=salian-franks" aria-label="Salian Franks on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4757 421 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Salian Franks lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5077 677L5304 942M5077 677L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5077 677h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5077 677h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tournai. <a href="/atlas?year=420&amp;focus=salian-franks">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
